   "updated_at": "2026-11-11T14:46:31Z",
   "body": "**Operator decision, 2026-11-11 (supersedes B1): the legacy group style everywhere.** The operator compared with legacy @ `87fe0d1c` on his device (Favoris, a category's topic list, the MP list). Legacy uses one style on all three:\n- **One rounded block per section.** Favoris has one per category, with the category headers outside the block. A category's topic list and the MP list each have a single block. In a category, the sub-forum picker and the Tous / Favoris / Suivis / Lus filter sit at the top of that same block.\n- **Rows inside the block are flat**, separated by thin inset lines.\n- **Highlighted rows** (favourite, flag colour) are drawn as rounded tinted pills, inset inside the block.\n- Unread badge on the right; the MP list has avatars on the left and a « non lu » chip.\n\nThe goal is consistency through **one row look and one block style**, not by removing the frame. This is legacy's look, so there is no deliberate gap: the PR cites legacy file:line. The device screenshots are kept locally and not posted here, since they show real pseudos.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
